  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The system's spatial accuracy was validated against interpolated point observations from a single municipality rather than directly observed pipe failure rates across multiple infrastructure networks.",
      "what": "An integrated decision support system combining the Analytic Hierarchy Process and spatial mapping was developed to prioritize sewer pipe rehabilitation across 18 physical and hydraulic indicators in Gdyel, Algeria. Evaluated under two prioritization scenarios, the framework identified that 13% of the network requires immediate intervention in the first scenario and 31% in the second. Spatial risk maps generated by the system matched continuous risk surfaces derived from local water utility diagnostic observations interpolated using Inverse Distance Weighted modeling.",
      "why": "This provides utility operators with a structured, multi-criteria workflow to target urgent sewer repairs when diagnostic budget constraints prevent complete network overhauls."
    }
  },
